{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_q2gWo9LCnXSTTzdCQjpxcWTM|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f7a1872087d2824883e8ba0a2baa","toolName":"read","args":{"path":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv:1-6"},"intent":"Confirm risk coverage"}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_q2gWo9LCnXSTTzdCQjpxcWTM|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f7a1872087d2824883e8ba0a2baa","toolName":"read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[risk_register.csv#8667]\n1:risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n2:R-001,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py OrderRepository.save opens a fresh SQLite connection and inserts into only the orders table; no backup, migration, durability policy, or retry is present.\",\"Data loss or failed writes may be unrecoverable; schema evolution is unmanaged.\",\"Define backup and migration strategy, configure SQLite durability expectations, and add bounded retry/transaction policy at the repository boundary.\",storage/platform\n3:R-002,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 order_event returns a dict only; handlers.py:13 and :20 return it in API responses; repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table.\",\"Creates and reads have no durable audit history, weakening compliance and incident investigation.\",\"Persist audit records in the same transaction as order mutations and define retention/query semantics.\",backend/security\n4:R-003,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults database_path to relative orders.sqlite and parses readonly; cli.py:8-10 reads settings but never enforces Settings.readonly.\",\"Working-directory changes select different databases, and configured readonly mode does not prevent writes.\",\"Require/resolve an explicit database location in deployment and enforce readonly in the repository or service write policy.\",platform/backend\n5:R-004,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order indexes payload['order_id'] and ['customer'] and applies int(payload['total_cents']) without schema, range, or semantic validation.\",\"Malformed requests raise KeyError/ValueError and invalid or nonsensical orders can reach storage without consistent API errors.\",\"Add request schema validation, constraints for IDs/customer/amount, and adapter-level 4xx error mapping.\",API/backend\n6:R-005,error handling and idempotency,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 propagates SQLite errors and enforces a primary key; handlers.py:6-13 has no duplicate handling or retry despite README.md:7.\",\"Duplicate or transient requests can fail as uncategorized errors and clients cannot safely determine retry behavior.\",\"Define duplicate/idempotency semantics, classify SQLite failures, and return stable API error responses with bounded retries where safe.\",API/storage\n7:"}],"details":{"totalLines":7,"displayContent":{"text":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR-001,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py OrderRepository.save opens a fresh SQLite connection and inserts into only the orders table; no backup, migration, durability policy, or retry is present.\",\"Data loss or failed writes may be unrecoverable; schema evolution is unmanaged.\",\"Define backup and migration strategy, configure SQLite durability expectations, and add bounded retry/transaction policy at the repository boundary.\",storage/platform\nR-002,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 order_event returns a dict only; handlers.py:13 and :20 return it in API responses; repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table.\",\"Creates and reads have no durable audit history, weakening compliance and incident investigation.\",\"Persist audit records in the same transaction as order mutations and define retention/query semantics.\",backend/security\nR-003,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults database_path to relative orders.sqlite and parses readonly; cli.py:8-10 reads settings but never enforces Settings.readonly.\",\"Working-directory changes select different databases, and configured readonly mode does not prevent writes.\",\"Require/resolve an explicit database location in deployment and enforce readonly in the repository or service write policy.\",platform/backend\nR-004,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order indexes payload['order_id'] and ['customer'] and applies int(payload['total_cents']) without schema, range, or semantic validation.\",\"Malformed requests raise KeyError/ValueError and invalid or nonsensical orders can reach storage without consistent API errors.\",\"Add request schema validation, constraints for IDs/customer/amount, and adapter-level 4xx error mapping.\",API/backend\nR-005,error handling and idempotency,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 propagates SQLite errors and enforces a primary key; handlers.py:6-13 has no duplicate handling or retry despite README.md:7.\",\"Duplicate or transient requests can fail as uncategorized errors and clients cannot safely determine retry behavior.\",\"Define duplicate/idempotency semantics, classify SQLite failures, and return stable API error responses with bounded retries where safe.\",API/storage\n","startLine":1,"lineNumbers":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]},"fileSize":2267,"meta":{"source":{"type":"path","value":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"}}}},"isError":false}
