er\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\", \"to\": \"sqlite3\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"to\": \"MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY\", \"type\": \"reads_config\"}\n  ],\n  \"key_functions\": [\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"description\": \"Maps MINISVC_DB to database_path (default orders.sqlite) and MINISVC_READONLY == 1 to readonly; returns frozen Settings.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"description\": \"Bootstraps the service repository and schema, then prints readiness and returns 0; argv is unused.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.__init__\", \"description\": \"Stores the configured database path as a pathlib.Path.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\", \"description\": \"Creates orders(order_id primary key, customer, total_cents) if absent using a SQLite transaction.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"description\": \"Inserts an Order into SQLite; duplicate IDs and other SQLite errors propagate; no retry is implemented.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"description\": \"Queries by order_id and reconstructs an Order or returns None.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"description\": \"Binds application adapter routes to create_order and get_order lambdas.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"description\": \"Indexes required payload keys, converts total_cents with int(), saves the order, and returns a created response with an in-memory event.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"description\": \"Reads an order and returns either missing or serialized order data plus an in-memory read event.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"description\": \"Constructs a dictionary event; does not write to a durable audit table.\"}\n  ],\n  \"runtime_flows\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CLI startup\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Executable minisvc resolves to minisvc.cli:main via pyproject.toml.\",\n        \"main reads os.environ and calls minisvc.config.load_settings.\",\n        \"load_settings selects MINISVC_DB or orders.sqlite and records MINISVC_READONLY.\",\n        \"main instantiates OrderRepository with settings.database_path.\",\n        \"main calls repo.init_schema, which creates the SQLite orders table if needed.\",\n        \"main prints minisvc ready at <database path> and returns 0.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"register_routes binds POST /orders to a lambda invoking create_order(payload, repo).\",\n        \"create_order reads order_id, customer, and total_cents from the payload.\",\n        \"total_cents is converted with int() and an Order is instantiated.\",\n        \"repo.save inserts the Order into SQLite in its own connection context.\",\n        \"order_event constructs an in-memory created event.\",\n        \"The handler returns status created, order_id, and event; no audit persistence or retry occurs.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},"intent":"Write module map JSON"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":811,"output":1951,"cacheRead":18176,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20938,"cost":{"input":0.0001622,"output":0.0023412,"cacheRead":0.00036352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00286692}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147485560,"responseId":"resp_081d756013a766ba016a94f71de8cc87d28c2db1de5aaa9e1f","duration":36544.405115,"ttft":1167.1719029999986},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xhMReJIhcRRuH1IOGv1XhcJT|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f71eb15c87d2ad3c765974af8935","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/module_map.json#BD6E]\nSuccessfully wrote 6748 bytes to out/module_map.json"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/module_map.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788147522146},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_h7YLcBm9zPsq51x3ilk5PpcR|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f7448ea087d28ee8d1df91832fe6","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write architecture summary","path":"/workspace/out/architecture.md","content":"# minisvc architecture\n\n## Scope\n\n`minisvc` is a small Python service that exposes order operations through an application adapter and provides a CLI bootstrap command. The fixture's code is authoritative over the older design notes in `README.md`.\n\n## Modules\n\n- `minisvc.config` (`config.py`): immutable `Settings` plus `load_settings(env)`. Reads `MINISVC_DB` (default `orders.sqlite`) and `MINISVC_READONLY` (true only when equal to `1`). The readonly value is currently loaded but not enforced anywhere.\n- `minisvc.models` (`models.py`): the `Order` dataclass (`order_id`, `customer`, `total_cents`).\n- `minisvc.storage.repo` (`storage/repo.py`): `OrderRepository`, a thin SQLite data-access layer. It creates the `orders` table, inserts orders, and fetches one order by ID.\n- `minisvc.audit` (`audit.py`): `order_event` creates a dictionary describing an order action. It does not persist an audit record.\n- `minisvc.api.handlers` (`api/handlers.py`): create and read handlers. `create_order` builds an `Order`, saves it, and formats a response. `get_order` reads and formats either a missing or successful response.\n- `minisvc.api.routes` (`api/routes.py`): `register_routes(app, repo)` binds `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/<order_id>` to handler callbacks.\n- `minisvc.cli` (`cli.py`): `main(argv=None)` loads environment settings, constructs a repository, initializes the schema, and reports readiness.\n\n`minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package marker files. They contain no business logic and should not be treated as architecture modules beyond package structure.\n\n## Entry points\n\nThe `pyproject.toml` script entry maps `minisvc` to `minisvc.cli:main`. The API integration entry point is `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`; it expects an external `app` object with `post` and `get` methods and a repository supplied by the caller. Its registered endpoints are:\n\n- `POST /orders` → `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`\n- `GET /orders/<order_id>` → `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`\n\n## Data flow\n\n### CLI startup\n\n`main` → `load_settings(os.environ)` → `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)` → `init_schema()` → readiness print. `Settings.readonly` is not passed to the repository or checked by any write path.\n\n### HTTP create order\n\n`POST /orders` callback → `create_order(payload, repo)` → required payload indexing and `int(total_cents)` → `Order` construction → `repo.save(order)` → `order_event(order, \"created\")` → response `{status, order_id, event}`. The event is response data only. SQLite writes use parameterized SQL and a context-managed connection.\n\nThe read path is similar: `GET /orders/<order_id>` → `repo.get` → either a `missing` response or an `ok` response containing `order.__dict__` and an in-memory `read` event.\n\n## Storage\n\nSQLite is the only persistence mechanism. `OrderRepository` opens a fresh connection for each schema, save, or get operation. The database path is configurable through `MINISVC_DB`; absent configuration uses a relative `orders.sqlite`, so the effective location depends on the process working directory. The schema has one `orders` table with a primary key on `order_id` and non-null `customer` and `total_cents` columns. There is no audit table, migration layer, explicit durability policy, or repository retry loop in this code.\n\n## Risks and extension points\n\n- **Readonly gap:** `load_settings` records readonly but `create_order` and `OrderRepository.save` never receive or enforce it. A caller expecting the README contract can still write.\n- **Failure handling:** malformed/missing payload fields, invalid integer conversion, SQLite errors, and duplicate IDs propagate from the handler; there is no HTTP error translation or retry behavior.\n- **Audit gap:** `order_event` is ephemeral and returned to clients. There is no durable audit trail or transaction tying an audit record to an order write.\n- **Runtime configuration:** relative database paths and direct `os.environ` access make deployment context significant. `main` also ignores `argv`.\n- **API boundary:** `create_order` performs only basic key access and integer coercion. Add explicit validation and adapter-level error mapping before exposing it to untrusted clients.\n\nNatural extension points are the repository boundary for transactions/migrations and the handler boundary for validation and response error policy. Readonly enforcement should be designed into that boundary rather than inferred from configuration alone; durable auditing should share the order-write transaction if audit completeness is required.\n"},"intent":"Write architecture summary"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2792,"output":1105,"cacheRead":18176,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22073,"cost":{"input":0.0005584,"output":0.001326,"cacheRead":0.00036352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00224792}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147522171,"responseId":"resp_081d756013a766ba016a94f742f3c887d2bf6e955940175b32","duration":22172.514028999998,"ttft":2424.591812999992},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_h7YLcBm9zPsq51x3ilk5PpcR|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f7448ea087d28ee8d1df91832fe6","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/architecture.md#4348]\nSuccessfully wrote 4606 bytes to out/architecture.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788147544350},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_lnPVYoZcp9oLSePsXF0yI0oJ|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f759577887d2972c85cd2ef5859f","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write discrepancy CSV","path":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","content":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths.\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads Settings.readonly, but minisvc/cli.py:9-10 does not pass it onward; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls OrderRepository.save unconditionally and storage/repo.py:17-22 always inserts.\",contradicted,\"Writes remain possible while readonly is configured, causing policy and data-integrity violations.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response.\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save exactly once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 has one sqlite3 connection and insert with no retry or error response conversion.\",contradicted,\"Transient database failures propagate and clients receive no defined retry/error behavior.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table.\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns a dict; handlers.py:13 and :20 place order_event output in the response, while storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table.\",\"contradicted\",\"Audit history is lost after the request and cannot support durable compliance or forensic review.\"\n\"The service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command.\",\"README.md:3\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 exposes minisvc.cli:main; api/routes.py:4-6 registers POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id>.\",confirmed,\"The documented high-level shape is accurate, subject to the adapter being supplied externally.\"\n"},"intent":"Write discrepancy CSV"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1878,"output":398,"cacheRead":20224,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22500,"cost":{"input":0.0003756,"output":0.00047759999999999995,"cacheRead":0.00040448000000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00125768}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147544355,"responseId":"resp_081d756013a766ba016a94f758a91887d2b9d980fc4b805ce0","duration":8155.171662000008,"ttft":1023.920437000008},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_lnPVYoZcp9oLSePsXF0yI0oJ|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f759577887d2972c85cd2ef5859f","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv#8920]\nSuccessfully wrote 1487 bytes to out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788147552519},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_VM4ypzKnnF29pBl8cQn7PySa|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f761800087d2aad751b30572b283","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write risk register CSV","path":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv","content":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR-001,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py OrderRepository.save opens a fresh SQLite connection and inserts into only the orders table; no backup, migration, durability policy, or retry is present.\",\"Data loss or failed writes may be unrecoverable; schema evolution is unmanaged.\",\"Define backup and migration strategy, configure SQLite durability expectations, and add bounded retry/transaction policy at the repository boundary.\",storage/platform\nR-002,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 order_event returns a dict only; handlers.py:13 and :20 return it in API responses; repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table.\",\"Creates and reads have no durable audit history, weakening compliance and incident investigation.\",\"Persist audit records in the same transaction as order mutations and define retention/query semantics.\",backend/security\nR-003,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults database_path to relative orders.sqlite and parses readonly; cli.py:8-10 reads settings but never enforces Settings.readonly.\",\"Working-directory changes select different databases, and configured readonly mode does not prevent writes.\",\"Require/resolve an explicit database location in deployment and enforce readonly in the repository or service write policy.\",platform/backend\nR-004,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order indexes payload['order_id'] and ['customer'] and applies int(payload['total_cents']) without schema, range, or semantic validation.\",\"Malformed requests raise KeyError/ValueError and invalid or nonsensical orders can reach storage without consistent API errors.\",\"Add request schema validation, constraints for IDs/customer/amount, and adapter-level 4xx error mapping.\",API/backend\nR-005,error handling and idempotency,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 propagates SQLite errors and enforces a primary key; handlers.py:6-13 has no duplicate handling or retry despite README.md:7.\",\"Duplicate or transient requests can fail as uncategorized errors and clients cannot safely determine retry behavior.\",\"Define duplicate/idempotency semantics, classify SQLite failures, and return stable API error responses with bounded retries where safe.\",API/storage\n"},"intent":"Write risk register CSV"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1289,"output":511,"cacheRead":21248,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23048,"cost":{"input":0.00025780000000000003,"output":0.0006131999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00042496,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00129596}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147552552,"responseId":"resp_081d756013a766ba016a94f760c18087d2923b3dd0d6f3d009","duration":10132.093076999998,"ttft":1016.6099200000026},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_VM4ypzKnnF29pBl8cQn7PySa|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f761800087d2aad751b30572b283","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/risk_register.csv#8667]\nSuccessfully wrote 2267 bytes to out/risk_register.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788147562690},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f5vnzpbZYqViIR7QXkQrjlYT|fc_081d756013a766ba016a94f76bc41487d2980fae6b41735dd7","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write onboarding plan","path":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","content":"# minisvc onboarding plan\n\n## Recommended read order\n\n1. `README.md` and `pyproject.toml` — stated intent and the `minisvc.cli:main` executable mapping. Treat the README design notes as claims to verify, not as behavior.\n2. `minisvc/config.py` — runtime settings and defaults.\n3. `minisvc/models.py` — the small `Order` data shape.\n4. `minisvc/storage/repo.py` — actual SQLite schema and persistence semantics.\n5. `minisvc/api/routes.py`, then `minisvc/api/handlers.py` — route wiring and request-to-storage flow.\n6. `minisvc/audit.py` — response-only event construction and its limits.\n7. `minisvc/cli.py` — how configuration and schema initialization are assembled at startup.\n\nThe three `__init__.py` files are package markers only: they are active for package discovery/import structure but contain no business logic. Focus debugging and changes on the modules above.\n\n## Local run and test commands\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\npython -m minisvc.cli\n```\n\nThe module currently defines `main` but does not invoke it under an `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` guard, so the installed script is the reliable CLI path:\n\n```bash\npython -m pip install -e .\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc-orders.sqlite minisvc\n```\n\nThere is no test suite or test configuration in this fixture. For a smoke check after installation, verify the command prints `minisvc ready at ...` and creates the SQLite database/table. API behavior requires an external adapter object implementing `post` and `get`; call `register_routes(app, repo)` with a temporary database to exercise route registration and handlers.\n\n## First debugging breakpoint / trace point\n\nSet the first breakpoint at `minisvc.api.handlers.create_order`, line 6, for a `POST /orders` request. Inspect the payload before `Order` construction, then step into `OrderRepository.save` (line 17) and `order_event` (line 4). This covers validation, persistence, and the documented-but-not-durable audit behavior in one trace. For startup-only issues, use `minisvc.cli.main`, line 8, and inspect `settings.database_path` and `settings.readonly`.\n\n## Safe first changes\n\n1. Add focused input validation and stable client-facing error mapping around `create_order`; preserve the existing repository interface and avoid changing schema behavior in the same change.\n2. Add an explicit readonly policy test and enforcement at the write boundary (`OrderRepository.save` or a clearly owned service policy), using `Settings.readonly` rather than adding a second configuration convention.\n\nBoth changes should be accompanied by tests once a test harness is introduced. Do not begin by editing package marker files; they are not runtime business logic.\n"},"intent":"Write onboarding plan"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":807,"output":662,"cacheRead":22272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23741,"cost":{"input":0.00016140000000000002,"output":0.0007944,"cacheRead":0.00044544,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00140124}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788147562720,"responseId":"resp_081d756013a766ba016a94f76b08d